    "title": "Teen charged in fatal Albuquerque shooting will stay in custody - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan Honeycutt No media credit provided. ,\n31 minutes ago\nALBUQUERQUE, N.M. (KRQE) – A teen charged in connection with a fatal robbery in September will stay in custody. According to the Bernalillo County District Attorney’s Office, the teen, along with several other teens, is accused of planning to rob 17-year-old Angelo Tafoya at an apartment complex on Tramway Boulevard . The teens planned to take Tafoya’s phone, gun, and drugs. Things escalated, and Tafoya was shot and killed. The DA’s Office said the group was in a stolen vehicle as well.\nNew Mexico State Police arrest Illinois murder suspect in Quay County The teen is facing a murder charge and is next scheduled for a hearing on November 24.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.",
